## for_over_a_number (exit 1)
error[Z0221]: `for` runs over a List, a Range or a list of variables, but this is an Int
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:10
  |
1 | for i in 5 {
  |          ^ not something to loop over
  |
  = help: write a list, `[1, 2, 3]`, a range, `1..200`, or `vars(lwage, hours)` for variables; a frame's rows are not looped over, its verbs work on them at once

## for_over_a_frame (exit 1)
error[Z0221]: `for` runs over a List, a Range or a list of variables, but this is a Frame
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:10
  |
2 | for r in d {
  |          ^ not something to loop over
  |
  = help: write a list, `[1, 2, 3]`, a range, `1..200`, or `vars(lwage, hours)` for variables; a frame's rows are not looped over, its verbs work on them at once

## for_over_a_range_of_variables (exit 1)
error[Z0221]: `for` cannot run over the range `x1..x3` outside a frame
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:10
  |
1 | for v in vars(x1..x3) {
  |          ^^^^^^^^^^^^ a range of variables
  |
  = help: a range is expanded against the frame it meets; name the variables one by one, `vars(x1, x2, x3)`

## list_for_without_a_value (exit 1)
error[Z0206]: this gives no value, so it cannot be put in a list
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:25
  |
1 | let xs = [for i in 1..3 {
  |                         ^ the body ends without a value
  |
  = help: `[for ...]` collects the value of its body's last expression in every pass; end the body with the value to collect, or drop the brackets

## let_shadows_loop_variable (exit 0)
10
20
warning[W0302]: `i` shadows the loop variable of the same name
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:9
  |
2 |     let i = i * 10
  |         ^ a `let` with a loop variable's name
  |
  = help: the loop variable is hidden until the block ends; a different name keeps both readable

## loop_variable_after_the_loop (exit 1)
error[Z0101]: nothing is called `i` here
 --> scripts/main.zeff:4:1
  |
4 | i
  | ^ not a binding
  |
  = help: a bare name is a binding made with `let`; text is written in quotes, and a variable is named inside a frame's method, as in `wages.mean(wage)`

## loop_variable_is_a_column (exit 1)
error[Z0106]: `x` is both the loop variable and a variable of d
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:18
  |
3 |     print(d.mean(x))
  |                  ^ which one is meant?
  |
  = help: rename the loop variable, or the column with `rename`; inside a frame method a loop variable wins over a column, so a clash is never resolved silently

## loop_variable_is_a_column_in_add (exit 1)
error[Z0106]: `y` is both the loop variable and a variable of d
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:21
  |
3 |     print(d.add(z = y * 2).n_rows())
  |                     ^ which one is meant?
  |
  = help: rename the loop variable, or the column with `rename`; inside a frame method a loop variable wins over a column, so a clash is never resolved silently

## break_outside_a_loop (exit 1)
error[Z0313]: `break` is only allowed inside a loop
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:1
  |
1 | break
  | ^^^^^ outside a loop
  |
  = help: use it in the body of a `for` loop

## continue_outside_a_loop (exit 1)
error[Z0313]: `continue` is only allowed inside a loop
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:1
  |
